The profile's one recording, assets/wordwinnow.gif, shows Wordwinnow, a
project of mine, analyzing two sentences of "A Scandal in Bohemia" by Arthur
Conan Doyle, and three sources besides my own work appear in it.

The text: the two sentences are in the public domain, as published in Standard
Ebooks' edition of The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes, whose editors dedicate
their own work to the public domain under CC0 1.0.

The levels: the two words' levels come from the CEFR-J Vocabulary Profile,
cited as its distributor asks: The CEFR-J Wordlist Version 1.5. Compiled by
Yukio Tono, Tokyo University of Foreign Studies.

The meanings: the definitions and related words come from WordNet 3.0, whose
license asks that its notice appear on every copy, so it follows.

